e the m1 chip to thank  as well for the smooth processing and  quick response time of the 2022 air  during my use of the 3d texture painting  tool i thought the ipad would lag  horrendously as my laptop usually does  when i'm rendering lighting and textures  with 3d models for school however  procreate and the 22 air allows me to do  rendering of everything lighting  textures and models seamlessly in 60  frames per second on top of that it  responds to any changes i make in real  time i can literally change the lighting  and paint new textures with zero lag  making this the smoothest and easiest  texture painting that i've done in a  very long time even on the 2020 model i  experienced zero lag time between  putting the tip of the apple pencil down  the screen and each joke i made allowing  my thoughts to flow freely onto the  screen however to my surprise procreate  on the 2022 air does not support as many  layers as the ipad pro despite having  the m1 chip at 300 dpi the 3d22 air  supports a maximum of 26 layers at a4  size 11 layers at a3 size and 120 layers  at a 4x6 photo size  this is in comparison to the numbers  from the ipad pro from a video last year  at dpi 300 44 layers at a3 size 92  layers at a4 size and 250 layers and the  4x6 photo size while these restraints  are right for me this might make the  2021 pro more suitable than the 2022 air  for artists handling layer heavy  projects while we're talking about more  technical topics i find that the m1 chip  does make a slight difference to  downloading and uploading speeds however  this is not very significant to me i  find that it only truly shines when  tackling graphics heavy applications or  taking a few apps running at the same  time without lagging any of them in  conclusion i highly recommend the 2022  ipad not just for artists like me  dabbling in different kinds of digital  art and media i recommend it to working  adults and students who are looking for  a compact device that can support their  